Resolves #22. I couldn't get it working using just a version from an extension as Gradle doesn't seem to allow using a lazily-evaluated provider of a Dependency instance. Open to suggestions if there's another way! This instead uses a public `CONFIGURATION_NAME`-named configuration that has a default dependency of the embedded version, but can be replaced with the user's own version if they wish.

```kotlin
dependencies {
  "sortDependencies"(some.newer.version)
}
```

